  "identifier": "hooknet",
  "name": "HookNet",
  "description": "Multi-resolution convolutional neural network for semantic segmentation of whole-slide histopathology images. Uses two parallel U-Net-style encoder-decoder branches operating at different magnifications (context and target), coupled via a 'hooking' mechanism that injects contextual feature maps into the detail branch. Demonstrated on multi-class tissue segmentation in breast cancer and TLS/germinal centre segmentation in lung cancer. MIT, TensorFlow 2.x, pip-installable. Published in Medical Image Analysis 2021. Developed by Diagnostic Image Analysis Group, Radboud University Medical Center.",
  "url": "https://github.com/DIAGNijmegen/pathology-hooknet",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/DIAGNijmegen/pathology-hooknet",
  "relatedLink": [
    "https://www.computationalpathologygroup.eu/software/hooknet/"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "keywords": [
